What then remains, Section 2 as amended and the disclaimer in
Section 7, under the copyright notice above, is the MIT License
(SPDX identifier: MIT), word for word. From that date copies of this
version may also carry the standard MIT License text in place of
this document.

This conversion is automatic, unconditional, and irrevocable, and
binds Licensor and its successors and assigns. It takes effect
whether or not Licensor republishes this version under a separate
MIT license file.

The same conversion happens immediately, without notice or any
further act, if for any period of 12 consecutive months Licensor
neither makes a public release of the Package nor provides any
security response to a responsibly reported vulnerability in it, or
if Licensor ceases business operations without a successor that
assumes this license.

The terms of this license, including the MIT Conversion Date, are
fixed for this version of the Software at its release and will never
change. Later versions of the Package may ship under revised terms;
