retroactively.


4. COUNTING COVERED REVENUE

"Control" means (i) the power, direct or indirect, to cause the
direction or management of an entity, whether by contract or
otherwise, (ii) ownership of fifty percent (50%) or more of an
entity's outstanding shares, or (iii) beneficial ownership of an
entity. Aggregation across common control exists solely to prevent
splitting one business across entities to multiply the
US $1,000,000 exemption; there is no other affiliate test in this
license. Aggregated Covered Revenue is counted once, and one
self-certification and payment by any of the aggregated entities
discharges condition (b) and Section 6 for all of them.

The fee is charged at most once for a product or service. It never
stacks across Licensor's other Clay-licensed packages used together
in one offering, across versions of the Software, or across copies
and instances, and revenue counted once under this or any other
Clay License is never counted again.

If the Software, a work derived from it, or a product or service
that contains it is one component of a larger product, service,
bundle, or subscription, whether or not that component is
separately priced or sold, its Covered Revenue is the portion of
the receipts fairly attributable to that component: its actual
standalone price if You also sell it on a standalone basis;
otherwise, any reasonable allocation method You apply consistently
in Your own financial statements or management accounts. An
allocation that complies with this paragraph binds Licensor for the
calendar year it covers, and allocated Covered Revenue never
exceeds the actual receipts of the whole.

Where the customer holds its own copy of the Software under this
license, Your receipts for installing, configuring, or maintaining
that copy are not Covered Revenue.


5. COVERAGE CERTIFICATES

At any time and at no charge, You may send Licensor, at the address
above, a complete and accurate written description of an offering
and, if applicable, a proposed allocation. Licensor shall respond
within 30 days with a written determination of whether, and to what
extent, receipts from the offering are Covered Revenue and whether
the allocation complies with Section 4. Silence for 30 days accepts
the request as submitted, except as to facts the request omitted or
misstated.

A determination, including a deemed acceptance, binds Licensor and
its successors for the versions of the Package it names, for as long
as the material facts described in the request remain accurate.


6. REPORTING, PAYMENT, AUDIT, AND CURE

If a fee is due under condition (b) for a calendar year, You shall,
within 90 days after the end of that year, send Licensor a
self-certification stating the Covered Revenue and the fee due, and
pay the fee through the address or URL in the License Details
above.

Licensor may audit the calculation at most once per calendar year,
at Licensor's expense, through an independent accountant under
confidentiality, on 30 days' written notice. If an audit finds
underpayment exceeding 5% of the amount due, You shall also
reimburse the reasonable cost of that audit.

A good-faith underpayment, late report, or late payment does not
terminate this license and is not copyright infringement; any
unpaid amount remains a debt owed to Licensor. If You fail to pay
or report as this section requires, Licensor shall give You written
notice, and You have 30 days from that notice to cure. Only a
failure to cure within those 30 days is a failure of condition (b).


